              "pts": [
                "<b>Problem 1: Naive `power(a, b)` vs. `FastPower(a, b)` (Lab 3 PDF pp. 1–2)</b>:<ul><li>Naive `a * power(a, b-1)` takes $T(b) = T(b-1) + 1 = \\Theta(b)$ multiplications.</li><li>`FastPower(a, b)` computes `c = a * a` and calls `ans = FastPower(c, ⌊b/2⌋)`, multiplying by an extra `a` only when $b$ is odd. After $k = \\log_2 b$ halving steps, $b / 2^k = 1$. Recurrence: $T(b) = T(b/2) + 1 \\implies \\mathbf{\\Theta(\\log b)}$ by Master Theorem Case 2 ($d = 0$).</li></ul>",
                "<b>Problem 2: Insertion Sort Recurrence $t_n = t_{n-1} + n$ (Lab 3 PDF pp. 3–4)</b>:<ul><li>Cannot be solved by the Master Theorem because the recursive term is $t_{n-1}$ (subtracting 1), not $t_{n/b}$ (dividing by $b$). Similarly, $T(n) = 2T(n/4) + T(n/2) + O(n)$ cannot be solved by the Master Theorem because it has mixed subproblem sizes.</li><li><b>Backward Substitution</b>: $t_n = t_{n-1} + n = t_{n-2} + (n-1) + n = \\dots = t_1 + 2 + \\dots + n = \\sum_{i=1}^n i = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} = \\Theta(n^2)$.</li></ul>"
              ]
