            "<b>Course Information (Slide 1.1)</b>: Taught by <b>Dr. Basheer Youssef</b> (two lectures per week + one lab). Primary textbooks: <i>Introduction to Algorithms</i> (CLRS, 3rd Ed.) and <i>Foundations of Algorithms Using C++ Pseudocode</i> (3rd Ed. — Neapolitan & Naimipour). Grading: <b>15 Midterm</b>, <b>15 Three Assignments</b>, <b>5 Labs</b>, <b>5 Two Quizzes</b>, and <b>60 Final</b>.",
            "<b>Definition of Analysis of Algorithms (Slide 1.3)</b>: The theoretical study of <b>computer-program performance</b> and <b>resource usage</b> (CPU time and memory space).",
            "<b>What is More Important Than Performance? (Slide 1.3)</b>: Correctness, modularity, maintainability, functionality, robustness, user-friendliness, programmer time, simplicity, extensibility, and reliability.",
            "<b>Why Study Algorithms and Performance? (Slide 1.4)</b>: (1) Algorithms determine <b>scalability</b>; (2) Performance draws the line between what is <b>feasible and impossible</b>; (3) Algorithmic mathematics provides a universal language for program behavior; (4) <b>Performance is the currency of computing</b>."
