              "ans": "• <b>(a) $\\Theta(m + n)$ Algorithm</b>: Merge $A$ and $B$ using the two-pointer merge subroutine until reaching index $(m + n)/2$.<br>• <b>(b) $O(\\log n)$ Algorithm ($m = n$)</b>: Compare the median $m_A = A[\\lfloor n/2 \\rfloor]$ and the median $m_B = B[\\lfloor n/2 \\rfloor]$ in $O(1)$ time:<br>  - If $m_A < m_B$, the overall median cannot be in the first half of $A$ or the second half of $B$; recursively find the median of $A[\\lfloor n/2 \\rfloor .. n-1]$ and $B[0 .. \\lceil n/2 \\rceil - 1]$.<br>  - If $m_A > m_B$, recursively find the median of $A[0 .. \\lceil n/2 \\rceil - 1]$ and $B[\\lfloor n/2 \\rfloor .. n-1]$.<br>  Recurrence: $T(n) = T(n/2) + O(1) = \\mathbf{O(\\log n)}$.",
