              "q": "<b>Qa (6 Marks)</b>: Write a top-down divide-and-conquer recursive C++ function that converts any array to a min-heap array in $O(n)$ time complexity. Trace your code on the array <code>[5, 7, 2, 1, 4, 3, 6]</code> by re-writing the array after each modification.",
              "ans": "<pre>void siftDown(int A[], int n, int i) {\n  int smallest = i, l = 2*i + 1, r = 2*i + 2;\n  if (l &lt; n &amp;&amp; A[l] &lt; A[smallest]) smallest = l;\n  if (r &lt; n &amp;&amp; A[r] &lt; A[smallest]) smallest = r;\n  if (smallest != i) {\n    swap(A[i], A[smallest]);\n    siftDown(A, n, smallest);\n  }\n}\nvoid buildMinHeapDC(int A[], int n, int i = 0) {\n  if (i &gt;= n / 2) return;          // leaf node\n  buildMinHeapDC(A, n, 2*i + 1);   // conquer left subtree\n  buildMinHeapDC(A, n, 2*i + 2);   // conquer right subtree\n  siftDown(A, n, i);               // combine in O(height)\n}</pre><b>Step-by-Step Trace on <code>[5, 7, 2, 1, 4, 3, 6]</code></b>:<br>1. Call on left child <code>i=1</code> (value <code>7</code>, children <code>1</code> at idx 3 and <code>4</code> at idx 4): swap <code>7 ↔ 1</code> $\\rightarrow$ <code>[5, 1, 2, 7, 4, 3, 6]</code>.<br>2. Call on right child <code>i=2</code> (value <code>2</code>, children <code>3</code> at idx 5 and <code>6</code> at idx 6): <code>2 &le; 3, 6</code> (no swap).<br>3. Call <code>siftDown</code> on root <code>i=0</code> (value <code>5</code>, children <code>1</code> and <code>2</code>):<br>   • Swap <code>5 ↔ 1</code> $\\rightarrow$ <code>[1, 5, 2, 7, 4, 3, 6]</code>.<br>   • Continue <code>siftDown</code> on <code>5</code> at idx 1 (children <code>7</code> at idx 3 and <code>4</code> at idx 4): swap <code>5 ↔ 4</code> $\\rightarrow$ <b>Final Min-Heap: <code>[1, 4, 2, 7, 5, 3, 6]</code></b>.",
