              "ans": "• <b>1. Linear Probing ($m=10$)</b>: <code>[0: 0, 1: 30, 2: 1, 3: 13, 4: -, 5: 55, 6: 16, 7: 26, 8: 28, 9: 9]</code>.<br>• <b>2. Quadratic Probing ($m=10$)</b>: <code>[0: 0, 1: 30, 2: 1, 3: 13, 4: -, 5: 55, 6: 16, 7: 26, 8: 28, 9: 9]</code>.<br>• <b>3. Double Hashing ($m=10, h_2(k)=5-(k\\bmod 5)$)</b>: <code>0→0; 30(h₁=0,h₂=5)→5; 1→1; 55(h₁=5,h₂=5)</code> probes $(5+5i)\\bmod 10 \\in \\{5, 0\\}$ (both full!) $\\implies$ <b>55 CANNOT BE INSERTED!</b> Remaining keys give <code>[0: 0, 1: 1, 2: -, 3: 13, 4: 26, 5: 30, 6: 16, 7: -, 8: 28, 9: 9]</code>.<br>• <b>4. Chaining ($m=10$)</b>: <code>0: [0, 30], 1: [1], 3: [13], 5: [55], 6: [16, 26], 8: [28], 9: [9]</code>.",
